IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part IV, "Offences" (s 44) and "Administrative Monetary Penalties" (s 44.1): the offence of a false or misleading
-- statement or of negotiating a cheque the person is not entitled to, the five-year limit for proceedings, and the Minister's power to
-- impose a penalty of up to $10,000 for each act or omission instead.
-- The text gives the punishment for the offence only as "punishable on summary conviction": it states no fine and no term of imprisonment, so the
-- rule for the greatest fine is NOTHING (NOTES.md, "What the text turns out to say").
-- Hohfeld: the Minister's power to impose a penalty (44.1(1)) is the person's liability; the person's duty to correct inaccuracies (5(6)) is the Minister's
-- claim, with the penalty behind it (44.1(1)(a.1)); the person's immunity from a second proceeding once a penalty is imposed (44(4)) is the Crown's disability.

§ `Offences`

-- s 44(1)(a): the first limb says "knowingly makes a false or misleading statement"; the second ("makes any such application or statement that by reason of
-- non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading") and the third ("obtains any benefit payment by false pretences") do not repeat the word "knowingly". The encoding
-- reads "knowingly" as governing only the first (fork OA1-F14 of NOTES.md).
-- src:1058 | (a) knowingly makes a false or misleading statement in any application or statement required or permitted by this Act or makes any such application or statement that by reason of any non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading or obtains any benefit payment by false pretences, or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44(1)(a) (src:1058)
GIVEN `the person knowingly makes a false or misleading statement in an application or statement required or permitted by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes an application or statement required or permitted by this Act that by reason of non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtains a benefit payment by false pretences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(1)(a): the person has done an act described in paragraph (a)` `the person knowingly makes a false or misleading statement in an application or statement required or permitted by this Act` `the person makes an application or statement required or permitted by this Act that by reason of non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading` `the person obtains a benefit payment by false pretences` MEANS
        `the person knowingly makes a false or misleading statement in an application or statement required or permitted by this Act`
    OR  `the person makes an application or statement required or permitted by this Act that by reason of non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading`
    OR  `the person obtains a benefit payment by false pretences`

-- src:1059 | (b) being the payee thereof, negotiates or attempts to negotiate any cheque to which that person is not entitled,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44(1)(b) (src:1059)
GIVEN `the person is the payee of a cheque` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person negotiates or attempts to negotiate the cheque` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not entitled to the cheque` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(1)(b): the person has done an act described in paragraph (b)` `the person is the payee of a cheque` `the person negotiates or attempts to negotiate the cheque` `the person is not entitled to the cheque` MEANS
        `the person is the payee of a cheque`
    AND `the person negotiates or attempts to negotiate the cheque`
    AND `the person is not entitled to the cheque`

-- src:1057 | 44 (1) Every person who
-- src:1058 | (a) knowingly makes a false or misleading statement in any application or statement required or permitted by this Act or makes any such application or statement that by reason of any non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading or obtains any benefit payment by false pretences, or
-- src:1059 | (b) being the payee thereof, negotiates or attempts to negotiate any cheque to which that person is not entitled,
-- src:1060 | (c) [Repealed, 1998, c. 21, s. 118]
-- src:1061 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44(1) (src:1057-1061)
GIVEN `the person has done an act described in paragraph 44(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has done an act described in paragraph 44(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(1): the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the person has done an act described in paragraph 44(1)(a)` `the person has done an act described in paragraph 44(1)(b)` MEANS
        `the person has done an act described in paragraph 44(1)(a)`
    OR  `the person has done an act described in paragraph 44(1)(b)`

-- The Act itself sets no figure for "punishable on summary conviction": NOTHING (the general law of summary conviction is outside the text).
-- src:1061 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44(1) (src:1061)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 44(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44(1): the greatest fine that this Act sets for the offence` `the person is guilty of an offence under subsection 44(1)` MEANS
    NOTHING

-- (2): no information or complaint "is open to objection on the ground that" it is for more than one matter or relates to more than one offence.
-- src:1063 | (2) No information or complaint for an offence under this Act is open to objection on the ground that the information or complaint is for more than one matter of complaint or that it relates to more than one offence.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44(2) (src:1063)
GIVEN `the information or complaint is for more than one matter of complaint or relates to more than one offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(2): the information or complaint is open to objection` `the information or complaint is for more than one matter of complaint or relates to more than one offence` MEANS
    FALSE

-- (3): "at any time within, but not later than, five years after the Minister becomes aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings".
-- "not later than, five years after": the same day five years on is still within the period (fork OA1-F15 of NOTES.md).
-- src:1065 | (3) Any proceedings under this Act in respect of an offence may be commenced at any time within, but not later than, five years after the Minister becomes aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44(3) (src:1065)
GIVEN `the day on which the Minister becomes aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(3): proceedings in respect of an offence may be commenced on the day` `the day on which the Minister becomes aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` `the day on which the proceedings are commenced` MEANS
        `the day on which the proceedings are commenced` AT LEAST `the day on which the Minister becomes aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings`
    AND `the day on which the proceedings are commenced` AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 5) `after` `the day on which the Minister becomes aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings`)

-- (4): no proceeding under section 44 or the Criminal Code if a penalty for the same act or omission has been imposed under section 44.1.
-- src:1067 | (4) No proceeding shall be commenced under this section or the Criminal Code for an act or omission if a penalty for that act or omission has been imposed under section 44.1.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44(4) (src:1067)
GIVEN `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed under section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(4): a proceeding may be commenced under this section or the Criminal Code for the act or omission` `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed under section 44.1` MEANS
    NOT `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed under section 44.1`

§ `Administrative Monetary Penalties`

-- s 44.1(1): the six acts or omissions, paragraphs (a), (a.1), (b), (c), (d) and (e), for which the Minister may impose a penalty.
-- src:1072 | (a) made a statement or declaration in an application or otherwise that the person knew was false or misleading;
-- src:1073 | (a.1) knowingly failed to correct any inaccuracies in the information provided by the Minister as required by subsection 5(6), 11(3.3), 15(2.4), 19(4.05) or 21(4.3);
-- src:1074 | (b) made a statement or declaration in an application or otherwise that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts;
-- src:1075 | (c) knowingly failed to declare to the Minister all or some of the person’s income;
-- src:1076 | (d) received or obtained by cheque or otherwise a benefit payment to which the person knew that they were not entitled, or a benefit payment that the person knew was in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which they were entitled, and did not return the cheque or the amount of the benefit payment, or the excess amount, as the case may be, without delay; or
-- src:1077 | (e) participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in any of paragraphs (a) to (d).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.1(1) (src:1072-1077)
