-- The power itself: the Minister "becomes aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish" one of the six.
-- src:1071 | 44.1 (1) The Minister may impose on a person a penalty for each of the following acts or omissions if the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister’s opinion establish that the person has
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.1(1) (src:1071)
GIVEN `the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that the person has done one of the following` IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `s 44.1(1): Facts about the person's acts or omissions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.1(1): the Minister may impose a penalty on the person` `the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that the person has done one of the following` facts MEANS
        `the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that the person has done one of the following`
    AND (    `s 44.1(1)(a): the person made a statement or declaration that the person knew was false or misleading` facts
         OR  `s 44.1(1)(a.1): the person knowingly failed to correct inaccuracies in the information provided by the Minister` facts
         OR  `s 44.1(1)(b): the person made a statement or declaration that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` facts
         OR  `s 44.1(1)(c): the person knowingly failed to declare income to the Minister` facts
         OR  `s 44.1(1)(d): the person received a benefit payment the person knew they were not entitled to and did not return it without delay` facts
         OR  `s 44.1(1)(e): the person participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in any of paragraphs (a) to (d)` facts)

-- (1.1): the purpose of the penalty.
-- src:1079 | (1.1) The purpose of the penalty is to promote compliance with this Act and not to punish.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.1(1.1) (src:1079)
`s 44.1(1.1): the purpose of the penalty` MEANS "to promote compliance with this Act and not to punish"

-- (2): "not more than $10,000" for each act or omission.
-- src:1081 | (2) The Minister may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than $10,000.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.1(2) (src:1081)
`s 44.1(2): the greatest amount of the penalty for each act or omission` MEANS 10000

-- src:1081 | (2) The Minister may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than $10,000.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.1(2) (src:1081)
GIVEN `the amount at which the Minister sets the penalty for the act or omission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.1(2): the Minister may set the amount of the penalty at the amount` `the amount at which the Minister sets the penalty for the act or omission` MEANS
    `the amount at which the Minister sets the penalty for the act or omission` AT MOST `s 44.1(2): the greatest amount of the penalty for each act or omission`

-- (3): no penalty if (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated, or (b) five years have passed since the day the Minister became aware.
-- Five years "have passed" at the end of the anniversary: the anniversary itself is still within the five years, as in s 44(3) (fork OA1-F15 of NOTES.md).
-- src:1083 | (3) A penalty shall not be imposed on a person under subsection (1) if
-- src:1084 | (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person; or
-- src:1085 | (b) five years have passed since the day on which the Minister became aware of the act or omission.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.1(3) (src:1083-1085)
GIVEN `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Minister became aware of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the penalty is imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.1(3): a penalty may be imposed on the person on the day` `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person` `the day on which the Minister became aware of the act or omission` `the day on which the penalty is imposed` MEANS
        (NOT `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person`)
    AND (NOT (`the day on which the penalty is imposed` GREATER THAN (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 5) `after` `the day on which the Minister became aware of the act or omission`)))

-- (4): the Minister may rescind or reduce the penalty on any of four grounds.
-- src:1087 | (4) The Minister may rescind the imposition of a penalty under subsection (1), or reduce the penalty,
-- src:1088 | (a) on the presentation of new facts;
-- src:1089 | (b) on being satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact;
-- src:1090 | (c) on being satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future; or
-- src:1091 | (d) on being satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.1(4) (src:1087-1091)
GIVEN `new facts are presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.1(4): the Minister may rescind the imposition of the penalty or reduce it` `new facts are presented` `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact` `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor` MEANS
        `new facts are presented`
    OR  `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact`
    OR  `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future`
    OR  `the Minister is satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor`
